IMDb wordmark
=============

File: imdb.svg
Downloaded: 2026-09-05, on the owner's explicit instruction.

Source
------
IMDb's own public brand page, https://brand.imdb.com/ , which offers a single
download, the IMDb Brand Toolkit:

  https://m.media-amazon.com/images/G/01/IMDb/brand/guidelines/imdb/IMDb_BrandToolkit_061925.zip
  (14,071,329 bytes, application/zip)

`imdb.svg` is one file taken from inside that archive, byte for byte:

  IMDb/IMDb SVG/IMDb_PrimaryLogo_Gold.svg

Nothing in the artwork was edited -- not the paths, not the viewBox, not the
colour (#F5C518). The archive also ships the usage guidelines as PDFs beside
the artwork (IMDb/IMDb PDF/), which is where the conditions live.

How it is used here
-------------------
Beside a rating the API attributes to IMDb, on the film page, at a size that
leaves the mark itself around 16px tall. The file keeps the clear space the
toolkit draws around the wordmark, so the rendered box is taller than the ink
-- that is deliberate, not padding to trim.

The mark is never used for a rating whose source the API has not named: a card
showing a bare number still shows a neutral star, because claiming a source we
were not given would be a lie about where the number came from.

IMDb is a trademark of IMDb.com, Inc. Its appearance here identifies the source
of a rating and implies no endorsement.
